          "guid": "mt23yolt0ozi7z34",
          "message": {
            "text": "overlay() owns the mount, so the render fn — not an imperative mount() — must read stage.value. The caller (completeReview) drives the modal by mutating the returned stage signal (completing → done/failed); because overlay() mount()s the render closure, reading stage.value inside it re-runs the mount on each transition with no explicit disposeMount to manage. The three click handlers delegate on handle.el (the persistent mount root), and handle.close() replaces the old backdrop-listener + disposeMount() teardown. This also newly enables Escape dismissal (covered by a new e2e in review-completion.test.ts).\n",
            "markdown": "`overlay()` owns the mount, so the render fn — not an imperative `mount()` — must read `stage.value`. The caller (`completeReview`) drives the modal by mutating the returned `stage` signal (completing → done/failed); because overlay() `mount()`s the render closure, reading `stage.value` inside it re-runs the mount on each transition with no explicit `disposeMount` to manage. The three click handlers delegate on `handle.el` (the persistent mount root), and `handle.close()` replaces the old backdrop-listener + `disposeMount()` teardown. This also newly enables Escape dismissal (covered by a new e2e in review-completion.test.ts).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/review/modal.tsx"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 112,
                  "endLine": 116,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  const handle = overlay(\n    () => <div className=\"modal\">{renderStage(stage.value)}</div>,\n    { className: 'modal-overlay', dismiss: ['escape', 'backdrop'], trap: true },\n  );\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
